{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>This is the statute of the Torah</b> — \"the statute of the Torah\" is juxtaposed to \"when you raise up its fat from upon it,\" hinting that the Torah was given only to eaters of the manna; secondarily, to eaters of terumah. And further hint: those who hold fast to the Torah of YHWH have portions [of terumah]; one does not give terumah to an ignoramus priest." "<b>You shall not profane</b> — and juxtaposed to it: \"the statute of the Torah,\" for a scholar who sins is a profanation of the Name." "<b>And you shall not die</b> — and juxtaposed to it: \"the statute of the Torah,\" as it is written: \"She is a tree of life to those who hold fast to her.\"" "<b>Red heifer</b> — in gematria: זה על עון עגל (this is upon the sin of the calf)." "<b>No yoke has come upon it</b> — על is written defective, for even if one did not draw it in a yoke but only mounted upon it alone, it is disqualified."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:34.088572249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}